# JavaScript style

- Use `const` and `let`. Never `var`. Prefer `const`.
- Compare with `===` / `!==`. Do not use `==` except `== null` when checking nullish.
- Treat all graph text as untrusted. Set `textContent`, never `innerHTML`, for titles, fields, and status labels.
- Source links: only `http:` / `https:` URLs, `target="_blank"`, and `rel="noopener noreferrer"`.
- Do not mutate the fetched graph. Keep expand / pan / zoom / colour mode in separate view state.
- Chevron is a `<button>`. Source link is an `<a>`. Give both an accessible name.
- If `graph.json` is missing or invalid, show the banner from the design doc. Do not render a half-built tree.
- One concern per function. Keep layout, rendering, and event handlers in named functions.

```javascript
// ❌ BAD
nodeEl.innerHTML = node.title;
state.graph.nodes[0].status = "Blocked";
if (url) link.href = url;

// ✅ GOOD
nodeEl.textContent = node.title;
state.expanded.add(node.id);
if (isHttpUrl(node.sourceUrl)) {
  link.href = node.sourceUrl;
  link.target = "_blank";
  link.rel = "noopener noreferrer";
}
```
